WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.306
Motivation tends to be stronger when effort connects to something a person values.

2
00:00:05.306 --> 00:00:12.245
That value may come from purpose, identity, usefulness, mastery, belonging, autonomy, or contribution to a real outcome.

3
00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:22.041
People are more likely to persist when they can see why the work matters and how their effort connects to something beyond simple compliance.

4
00:00:22.041 --> 00:00:26.531
Autonomy, competence, and belonging are useful ideas for practical motivation design.

5
00:00:26.531 --> 00:00:31.837
Autonomy means people have some meaningful control over how they approach the work.

6
00:00:31.837 --> 00:00:35.919
Competence means they can see a path to getting better.

7
00:00:35.919 --> 00:00:42.041
Belonging means the social environment supports participation instead of making people feel isolated or disposable.

8
00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:47.756
These conditions do not make work effortless, but they make effort feel more reasonable.

9
00:00:47.756 --> 00:00:49.796
Meaning should be handled carefully.

10
00:00:49.796 --> 00:00:55.103
People notice when purpose language is fake, inflated, or disconnected from actual conditions.

11
00:00:55.103 --> 00:01:04.490
Empty slogans can backfire if the day-to-day system rewards speed over quality, punishes questions, or ignores the real constraints people face.

12
00:01:04.490 --> 00:01:13.878
Motivation is stronger when the stated purpose matches the work environment and when leaders remove barriers rather than only asking for more commitment.

13
00:01:13.878 --> 00:01:19.184
In learning and workplace performance, relevance is often the first bridge to meaning.

14
00:01:19.184 --> 00:01:25.307
People need to understand how a skill, process, or decision connects to their actual responsibilities.

15
00:01:25.307 --> 00:01:29.797
When the connection is real, motivation becomes less dependent on hype.

16
00:01:29.797 --> 00:01:42.450
Learners and workers can say, this is worth effort because it helps me solve a real problem, protect a real outcome, or become more capable in a direction I care about.
